{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>As sockets for their bars.</b> The rings that you make in them shall be houses — to receive the bars into them." "<b>And you shall overlay the bars with gold.</b> Not that the gold was affixed onto the bars — they had no overlay at all — but in the board he would fix a kind of two tubes of gold, like the two sides of a hollow reed, and fix them at the ring on each side; their length spans the width of the board from the ring on this side and from it on that side. The bar enters into it, and from it into the ring, and from the ring into the second opening — so the bars are found overlaid with gold when they are inserted in the boards. And these bars protruded from outside; the rings and the tubes were not visible inside the Tabernacle — rather, the entire wall was smooth on the inside."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:49.559017948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}